WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.069
Module five. How a vendor adds stock, and when products become visible to customers.

2
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.726
The vendor is approved. Now they need to start selling.

3
00:00:11.726 --> 00:00:13.110
This module shows how.

4
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.437
We'll start with the warehouses page.

5
00:00:15.887 --> 00:00:18.426
Then adding an SKU, field by field.

6
00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:21.372
Why a product can be invisible to customers.

7
00:00:21.822 --> 00:00:25.064
Stock status: in stock, low stock and out of stock.

8
00:00:25.514 --> 00:00:28.416
And the difference between hiding and deleting a product.

9
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.902
This is the vendor's warehouses page. At the top: active warehouses, total capacity,

10
00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.227
Open orders and total SKUs live.

11
00:00:39.677 --> 00:00:44.955
Each warehouse card shows its status. A new or edited warehouse shows Pending until

12
00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:46.354
The admin approves it.

13
00:00:46.804 --> 00:00:51.071
Approved means products in this warehouse can be shown to nearby customers.

14
00:00:51.521 --> 00:00:55.355
And Add warehouse lets an approved vendor add more locations.

15
00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.366
Each new one needs approval too.

16
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.644
Adding stock takes five steps.

17
00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:04.526
Go to Inventory, and click Add SKU.

18
00:01:04.976 --> 00:01:08.944
Filter by category, and select the product from the master catalog.

19
00:01:09.394 --> 00:01:11.442
Choose which warehouse the stock is in.

20
00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:14.879
Enter the stock quantity, and the minimum order quantity.

21
00:01:15.329 --> 00:01:20.918
Check the warranty and return policy, choose cash on delivery, and click Create SKU.

22
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:25.253
Let's watch this in the live demo.

23
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:34.358
The vendor has one warehouse, Central City. Now Inventory, then Add new SKU.

24
00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:55.276
Filter by category. Only the vendor's approved categories appear.

25
00:01:55.276 --> 00:02:00.523
Safety equipment is chosen, then the product: 3M industrial safety helmet.

26
00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:15.214
The warehouse is selected, then stock quantity and minimum order quantity.

27
00:02:15.214 --> 00:02:16.811
Minimum order is one here.

28
00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:27.744
Warranty and return policy come from the master listing.

29
00:02:27.744 --> 00:02:32.587
The vendor can request a change, with a reason, but the admin must approve it.

30
00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:48.313
The SKU is created, and it appears in product inventory, with its warehouse, price,

31
00:02:48.313 --> 00:02:49.878
Stock level and status.

32
00:02:51.677 --> 00:02:53.448
Let's look closer at each field.

33
00:02:53.898 --> 00:02:58.137
The product always comes from the master catalog, and only from the vendor's

34
00:02:58.137 --> 00:02:59.252
Approved categories.

35
00:02:59.702 --> 00:03:02.156
The warehouse is where this stock physically sits.

36
00:03:02.606 --> 00:03:06.060
Stock quantity is the number of units available to sell.

37
00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.280
Keep it honest, or orders will fail.

38
00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.708
Minimum order quantity is the smallest amount a customer can buy.

39
00:03:12.708 --> 00:03:16.197
For example, bricks might have a minimum of five hundred.

40
00:03:16.647 --> 00:03:20.274
Any policy change request needs a reason, and admin approval.

41
00:03:20.724 --> 00:03:25.289
And allow COD turns cash on delivery on or off for this SKU.

42
00:03:27.677 --> 00:03:32.452
Remember this rule. No seller, no listing. A product in the master catalog stays

43
00:03:32.452 --> 00:03:37.226
Hidden from customers until at least one vendor adds it to an approved warehouse

44
00:03:37.226 --> 00:03:41.882
Near them. So if someone says, I can't see the product in the app, check three

45
00:03:41.882 --> 00:03:46.597
Things: does a vendor have it in stock, is their warehouse approved, and is the

46
00:03:46.597 --> 00:03:48.328
Customer near that warehouse.

47
00:04:35.677 --> 00:04:37.597
Let's watch this in the live demo.

48
00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:46.110
Here's the problem from the demo. The helmet was added, but it wasn't showing in the

49
00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.789
App for a customer in Lucknow.

50
00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:09.109
The reason: the Central City warehouse was pinned in Bengaluru.

51
00:05:09.109 --> 00:05:11.106
So the vendor edits the warehouse.

52
00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:35.757
The location is changed to Lucknow on the map, and the vehicles are kept.

53
00:05:56.610 --> 00:06:01.555
Notice the status is now Pending. The admin approved the new location, and then the

54
00:06:01.555 --> 00:06:03.223
Product appeared in the app.

55
00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:18.464
Good to know. When a vendor edits a warehouse location, the warehouse goes back to

56
00:06:18.464 --> 00:06:22.716
Pending. Products in it are hidden until the admin approves it again.

57
00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:27.277
So after any location change, remind the admin team to approve it quickly.

58
00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:11.335
In inventory, every SKU has a stock status. There's a breakdown at the top of the

59
00:07:11.335 --> 00:07:11.663
Page.

60
00:07:12.113 --> 00:07:14.588
In stock means there are enough units to sell.

61
00:07:15.038 --> 00:07:18.793
Low stock means it's running low, so the vendor should restock soon.

62
00:07:19.243 --> 00:07:24.341
And out of stock means zero units. Customers can't order it until stock is added.

63
00:07:26.743 --> 00:07:30.818
Now, in the admin catalog, there are two ways to take a product down.

64
00:07:31.268 --> 00:07:35.601
The inactive toggle hides the product from both vendors and customers.

65
00:07:35.601 --> 00:07:38.820
It can be switched back on any time. Use this first.

66
00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:44.080
Delete is permanent, and it's blocked while any order for that product is ongoing.

67
00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.014
Once those orders are complete, delete is allowed.

68
00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.330
Let's watch this in the live demo.

69
00:07:55.143 --> 00:07:58.585
This is a product's detail view in the admin catalog.

70
00:07:58.585 --> 00:08:03.975
At the bottom: vendors offering this product. Here, no vendor has listed it yet, so

71
00:08:03.975 --> 00:08:05.468
Customers can't see it.

72
00:08:23.943 --> 00:08:26.919
Back in the list, the status toggle is switched.

73
00:08:26.919 --> 00:08:30.578
A message says product deactivated, then product activated.

74
00:08:58.343 --> 00:09:00.263
Let's watch this in the live demo.

75
00:09:05.677 --> 00:09:09.154
Now a delete is tried on a product that has an ongoing order.

76
00:09:32.077 --> 00:09:35.024
It can't be deleted while the order is in progress.

77
00:09:35.024 --> 00:09:37.624
Once the order is complete, delete will work.

78
00:10:08.877 --> 00:10:13.570
This is the checklist to use when a vendor says, I can't see my product in the app.

79
00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:17.092
Is the SKU created, with stock above zero?

80
00:10:17.542 --> 00:10:19.910
Is the warehouse approved, and not pending?

81
00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.302
Is the warehouse pin in the right city?

82
00:10:22.752 --> 00:10:25.205
Is the product active in the admin catalog?

83
00:10:25.655 --> 00:10:28.343
And is the customer actually near that warehouse?

84
00:10:30.743 --> 00:10:35.212
Quick check. A vendor moved their warehouse pin to Lucknow, and their products

85
00:10:35.212 --> 00:10:36.759
Vanished from the app. Why?

86
00:10:40.709 --> 00:10:44.427
Because editing the location sends the warehouse back to pending.

87
00:10:44.427 --> 00:10:47.344
Once the admin approves it, the products come back.

88
00:10:50.143 --> 00:10:51.700
Let's sum up module five.

89
00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:57.454
Adding an SKU means choosing the product, warehouse, stock, minimum order and cash

90
00:10:57.454 --> 00:10:58.230
On delivery.

91
00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:01.688
Policy changes need a reason and admin approval.

92
00:11:02.138 --> 00:11:05.168
No seller in an approved warehouse means no listing.

93
00:11:05.618 --> 00:11:08.306
Location edits send a warehouse back to pending.

94
00:11:08.756 --> 00:11:13.219
And prefer inactive over delete. Delete is blocked during orders.

95
00:11:13.219 --> 00:11:15.348
Next up: price change requests.

96
00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:22.628
That's the end of module 5. Next up, module 6: Price change requests.
